[{"items":["1.1. Business Development and consultation:
• Researching and identifying potential new business opportunities;
• Contributing information, ideas, opinions and suggestions, as well as creative and effective answers to client issues and needs;
• Developing new ideas and business pitches for new and existing clients.
Consult and coach business models","1.2. Account Management:
1.2.1. Project management
• Building up & retaining good relationship with clients to meet their business needs on time and in satisfactory manner;
• Actively contributing to clients’ and team meetings, as well as in brainstorming, developing and researching for client’s projects;
• Being in charge of continuous communication with clients and actively providing appropriate consultancy to clients;
• Being in-charge of building Integrated Marketing Communications plan as well as individual event and PR planning for internal and external accounts.
• Be familiar with different types of proposal formats and communications tools/concepts, which guarantee the best plans proposed to clients;
• Being in-charge of managing vendors and suppliers in implementing approved plans for events, PR and other integrated marketing communication initiatives;
• Building and managing skillful and strong Teams in HCMC;
• Demonstrating knowledge and understanding of company vision, values and structure, including the full range of company products, services and capabilities.

1.2.2. Initiative and Problem Solving:
• Familiarizing with, and supporting achievement of the Company’s vision and goals, and amplifying the Company’s values;
• Actively identifying and handling internal issues;
• Recommending solutions when problems arise;
• Attending and contributing to team, Company, group and office meetings, if any;
• Displaying work ethic and values of the firm in day-to-day behavior.

1.2.3. Financial Management:
• Responsible for the financial contributions of multiple clients businesses (if applicable) including revenue, resource allocation/expenses, invoicing, collecting bad debt, margin improvement, contract negotiations/development
• Deliver on preset gross profit objectives Coordinate project estimates internally and gain client approval on pricing
• Manage internal project costs against budgets (P &L target at least 32% of the contract value)"],"title":"SCOPES OF WORKS"}]
